<title>JAPAN: Daiichi Pharm shares fall on downgrading.</title>
<headline>Daiichi Pharm shares fall on downgrading.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Daiichi Pharmaceutical Co Ltd lost ground on Wednesday morning after the firm's downgrade by a foreign securities house, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0105 GMT, the share was down 50 yen at 1,920. Turnover was 561,000 shares.  </p>
<p>Lehman Brothers Japan Inc said in a report issued on Tuesday that it had downgraded Daiichi Pharmaceutical's shares to &quot;3&quot; from &quot;2&quot;, due to a delay in one of the company's new drugs.</p>
</text>
